3.2.2 Subacute oral toxicity study
3.2.2.1 Clinical observations
Subacute oral toxicity study on SG was performed for 28-day in a graded range of doses: 500 mg/kg, 1,000 mg/kg and 2000 mg/kg body weight. No mice died throughout the period of the study and no abnormal behavioural signs were noted prior to sacrifice. All mice exhibited body weight gain throughout the study (
Figure 3A
). The changes in the body weight of mice administered SG did not differ significantly with the control group, except for the male mice group administered 2000 mg/kg SG. Significant weight loss was initially observed for that group after 2 weeks of study, but the changes were within an acceptable range, i.e., ∼10%, and they recovered at week 3 and continued to gain weight until the end of study (
Figures 3A,B
). Meanwhile, the body temperature of mice from different groups did not vary significantly from each other, and weekly food consumption displays a large fluctuation between groups, but the trend is consistent between groups (
Figures 3C,D
).
