3.2.2.2 Haematological parameters
Haematological results are summarized in
Table 3
. There were no observed significant effects of SG on haematological parameters in female mice. However, in male mice, 1,000 mg/kg SG caused a significant increase in WBC, which is attributed to the increase in GRA counts (
p
< 0.001 and
p
< 0.001, respectively). Similarly, 2,000 mg/kg SG caused an increase in GRA counts but to a lesser extent than that of 1,000 mg/kg (
p
< 0.01).
